everity=serious | problem=QA gate is placed AFTER the critic gate (line ~4432) but BEFORE the coder-bypass gate (line ~4453). If plannerStatus is DONE but the coder-bypass gate later resets it to CONTINUE, the QA gate has already run and passed on a state that gets invalidated. The QA verdict is lost — the task goes back to CONTINUE without re-running QA after the bypass fix.; file=driver.ps1 | line=+      $conversationSummary = Read-Summary | severity=serious | problem=Read-Summary is called without error handling. If the summary file is locked, corrupted, or missing, Read-Summary may throw (it uses Get-Content -Raw). The outer try/catch is empty, so checkpoint write silently fails. This is a mask — the checkpoint feature degrades without any log.; file=config.json | line=+    "useLLMPriority": false | severity=serious | problem=New config key added but no code in the diff reads it. The Invoke-BacklogLLMPrioritize function always runs if called; there's no gating on this flag. Either the flag is dead config (confusing operators) or the gating code is in the truncated part of the diff. If the curator calls Invoke-BacklogLLMPrioritize unconditionally, the flag is ignored.; file=lib/backlog.ps1 | line=+        $raw = Invoke-LLM -Purpose 'prioritizer' -Prompt $prompt -TimeoutSec 30 -Temperature 0.2 | severity=minor | problem=TimeoutSec=30 may be too short for LLM prioritization of 20 items. DeepSeek API can take 15-45 seconds for large prompts. If timeout fires, the function returns 0 and silently fails — no prioritization happens, but the operator won't know why.; file=lib/backlog.ps1 | line=+      $allItems | | severity=minor | problem=Get-Backlog is called, then filtered with Where-Object. If the backlog has 500+ items, this loads everything into memory and filters in PowerShell (slow). The LLM call then processes up to $MaxItems (20) items — the filtering could be done with a limit in the query if Get-Backlog supports it.
