2026-05-30T15:23:12  model=deepseek-v4-pro verdict=FAIL severity=serious crc=0 | [Автозадача из бэклога] [deep-agent/reliability-model/deepseek-v4-flash] missing | Мьютекс-проверка в Stop-BridgeJob гоняется с PID recycling и не устраняет корневую причину — требовались Job Objects; также не исправлен 2>&1 в раннере и нет гарантии BOM для нового файла. | MUTEX IDENTITY VERIFICATION IS RACE-PRONE AND DOES NOT FIX ROOT CAUSE: The mutex-based identity check in Stop-BridgeJob has a critical race condition. Between the mutex acquisition check and the taskkill call, the original process can exit and a new process can recycle the same PID. The mutex WaitOne(0) returning false only proves the mutex was held at that instant, not that the process holding it is the same one that started the job. This is structurally similar to the original PID+startTicks verification (both are time-of-check-to-time-of-use races) and does not address the fundamental PID recycling problem. The task description explicitly recommended using Windows Job Objects which would atomically terminate the entire process tree without any identity verification races. This diff patches the symptom with another heuristic check rather than fixing the root cause.; COMMIT MESSAGE OVER-CLAIM: The commit message claims 'missing-cleanup' fix but the diff only adds a mutex check that is itself racy. No evidence of testing with actual PID recycling scenarios is present in the code or commit. The mutex approach was not the recommended solution (Job Objects were) and the diff does not explain why the more robust approach was rejected.; STDERR REDIRECTION IN RUNNER SCRIPT STILL USES 2>&1: The runner script in Start-BridgeJob still uses '*>> $log 2>&1' which under PowerShell 5.1 wraps each stderr line in NativeCommandError ErrorRecord objects, potentially corrupting the log output or causing silent failures. This was a known issue mentioned in the audit instructions but was not addressed.; NEW FILE tools/live-status.ps1 LACKS BOM VERIFICATION: The diff shows the file starts with '﻿' (BOM marker) but this is only visible in the diff header. The actual file creation via git add does not guarantee BOM preservation on all systems. No explicit BOM verification or encoding enforcement is present in the script itself or in the build process for this new file.
